// The model's ratings and the readings are the red one's. Yellow, green, blue and white set their own.
{
  "format": 4,
  "part": "led-5mm",
  "version": "0.3.0",
  "title": "5 mm LED",
  "summary": "Round 5 mm through-hole LED, two leads on 2.54 mm. The longer lead is the anode. Pick its color: red, yellow, green, blue or white. Red, yellow and green are diffused; blue and white are water clear. Red, yellow, blue and white warn above 30 mA, green above 25 mA. Red and yellow warn above 75 mW, green above 62.5 mW, and blue and white above 120 mW. The page's glow is the mean current since the last frame, so a PWM-dimmed LED glows at its average. Red, yellow and green glow fully at 10 mA, and blue and white at 20 mA, the currents their datasheets rate light at. Red, yellow and green are off at or below 100 uA, and blue and white at or below 500 uA.",
  "tags": ["led", "light", "indicator", "through-hole"],
  "license": "MIT OR Apache-2.0",
