  "not_simulated": [
    { "what": "light", "why": "The engine reports current, not luminous intensity. Each color's glow is 1 at the current its datasheet rates luminous intensity at, 10 mA for red, yellow and green and 20 mA for blue and white, and blooms above that. The colors' intensities at that current differ and are not modeled. Each color's forward curve is fitted from 2 mA to 20 mA as its source names. Below 2 mA and above 20 mA the current is that curve extended. A threshold at 1 mA would sit outside the fit. Luminous intensity versus forward current is drawn as a straight line from 0 mA on each datasheet, so the extended current still glows in proportion." },
    { "what": "temperature", "why": "The fits are at 25 C and the engine has no temperature." },
    { "what": "reverse breakdown", "why": "The engine's LED has no breakdown voltage." },
  ],
}
